{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00015",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.23,
      "end_seconds": 7.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.79,
      "text": "Well, good evening, doctor, thank you for staying late."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.64,
      "end_seconds": 12.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "right on time. Sit, please. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 14.96,
      "end_seconds": 21.48,
      "duration_seconds": 6.52,
      "text": "Well, hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.24,
      "end_seconds": 29.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.33,
      "end_seconds": 34.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "I've been passing out once last week"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.32,
      "end_seconds": 38.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "Tell me what you take day to day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.03,
      "end_seconds": 44.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "Amlodipine. I take it 5 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 46.21,
      "end_seconds": 55.14,
      "duration_seconds": 8.93,
      "text": "He is supposed to take it once a day, but I can't say he always does."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.48,
      "end_seconds": 67.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "when did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.18,
      "end_seconds": 73.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "Uh, it's been five days, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.84,
      "end_seconds": 78.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Does it happen all the time or in spells?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.52,
      "end_seconds": 81.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "It's on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.64,
      "end_seconds": 87.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "alright, does it come along with anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.56,
      "end_seconds": 105.7,
      "duration_seconds": 16.14,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get blurred vision beforehand as well. Hmm, and there's a bit of lightheadedness since then as well, two weeks now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.61,
      "end_seconds": 109.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "And how severe is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.34,
      "end_seconds": 115.39,
      "duration_seconds": 5.05,
      "text": "maybe a six out of ten on a bad day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.22,
      "end_seconds": 118.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Is it mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.71,
      "end_seconds": 122.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Moderate, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.1,
      "end_seconds": 129.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.31,
      "text": "Have you been passing out once last week at any time before this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.03,
      "end_seconds": 138.82,
      "duration_seconds": 7.79,
      "text": "a bit, a couple of years ago it it settled by itself back then"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.86,
      "end_seconds": 146.73,
      "duration_seconds": 6.87,
      "text": "have you had any loss of bladder control, chest pain or shaking or jerking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.69,
      "end_seconds": 150.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.24,
      "end_seconds": 156.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "Did you get confusion afterwards, palpitations or tongue biting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.19,
      "end_seconds": 162.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "No, uh, I'd have mentioned it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.37,
      "end_seconds": 167.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.54,
      "end_seconds": 171.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "No, that that side's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.64,
      "end_seconds": 195.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.89,
      "end_seconds": 204.31,
      "duration_seconds": 7.42,
      "text": "I, I have high blood pressure, for five years yes, arthritis in my knees"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.56,
      "end_seconds": 215.58,
      "duration_seconds": 7.02,
      "text": "uh-huh alright, arthritis in your knees, that matches what I have here do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.3,
      "end_seconds": 222.05,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "I used to smoke but I quit five years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.46,
      "end_seconds": 224.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "how's your diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 226.65,
      "end_seconds": 228.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "I'm mostly vegetarian."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.68,
      "end_seconds": 231.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "Any sport or activity?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.37,
      "end_seconds": 234.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "I play badminton on Sundays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.32,
      "end_seconds": 239.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Does anything run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.89,
      "end_seconds": 244.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "I mean, um, my brother has asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.68,
      "end_seconds": 250.88,
      "duration_seconds": 5.2,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 252.81,
      "end_seconds": 257.91,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "Okay, you know, so yes, aspirin. I get wheezing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.11,
      "end_seconds": 262.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "let me check your vitals now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.95,
      "end_seconds": 272.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "rest your hand here.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.77,
      "end_seconds": 304.67,
      "duration_seconds": 10.9,
      "text": "Okay: temp 36.8 degrees, heart rate 72, BP is 123 over 76. And respiratory rate 16, SpO2 97 percent on room air."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 305.86,
      "end_seconds": 307.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.85,
      "end_seconds": 313.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "I'll come back to those numbers"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.14,
      "end_seconds": 318.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Shall we do the examination?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.15,
      "end_seconds": 325.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.16,
      "text": "No problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.14,
      "end_seconds": 329.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "hold that position for me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 344.45,
      "end_seconds": 352.14,
      "duration_seconds": 7.69,
      "text": "your pulse is regular and there's a small bruise on the right side of the head"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.03,
      "end_seconds": 355.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "bear with me a second"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 366.5,
      "end_seconds": 368.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "No murmurs on listening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 369.4,
      "end_seconds": 370.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Yes, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 373.41,
      "end_seconds": 375.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "That's fine, sit up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 388.86,
      "end_seconds": 401.88,
      "duration_seconds": 13.02,
      "text": "So, based on the history and the examination, I can't pin this down yet. We're looking at a a simple faint, probably reflex-related or a heart rhythm problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 402.76,
      "end_seconds": 409.44,
      "duration_seconds": 6.68,
      "text": "I've been thinking the worst, to be honest. Is it bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 409.97,
      "end_seconds": 442.15,
      "duration_seconds": 32.18,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a simple faint, probably reflex-related, and we'll know more once the an echocardiogram is back. I think an echocardiogram makes sense here, for syncope. We should do blood tests for syncope. Drink enough water and avoid standing still for long stretches, and sit if you feel it coming. If you smoke, this is a good moment to think about stopping, and we can help you with that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 443.7,
      "end_seconds": 456.64,
      "duration_seconds": 12.94,
      "text": "Let's hold off on an ECG for now, and if there's no change next month we can revisit it. Let's plan a check in two weeks. Any last questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 461.03,
      "end_seconds": 465.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "one thing: no, actually that's all thanks"
    }
  ]
}